From what I understood, the odds of getting a potion of booze from the
horn of plenty (using an unicorn horn if needed) are ;
1 in 13 chance of a potion, times :
  1 in 28 chance for booze, plus
  1 in 28 chance for fruit juice, plus
  1 in 28 chance for sickness, plus
  22 in 28 chance that the potion is magical, times
     1 in 5 chance that it is replaced by booze, plus
     1 in 5 chance that it is replaced by fruit juice
     (Never sickness)

1/13 * (3/28 + (22/28 * 2/5)) = 59 chances out of 1820 to get booze.

Assuming you always wait until the horn is under 10 charges to charge
it, and use blessed charging, it will add 10 to 15 charges (average
12,5) each time. This makes an average of 295/728 (about 0.4) potions
of booze per use of the PYEC. If rnz(100) is fair with you, you can
use it every 100 turns. So you have one potion of booze every 250
turns.

If you spent a wish to get the HoP, you'll want to get at least 2
wishes out of it. Since you already summoned a djinni, it will take on
average (assuming you bless them) over 40 smoky potions, i.e. over
10,000 turns (or much more, since I underrated rnz(100)). Are you sure
you want to do this ?


